### Step P2-007: Channel Permissions Configuration
**Goal:** Set per-channel permissions: Samm full access, bot write, evidence write-only.
**Dependencies:** P2-006 | **Cost:** $0 | **ADR:** ADR-022 | **AC:** AC-SEC-001 | **Time:** 1h

**Context:** Channel permissions enforce information boundaries. Samm has full access everywhere. The bot can post in all channels. Evidence channels are write-only for automated posting.

**Commands:**
```bash
cd /home/guinevere/code/guinevere
source .venv/bin/activate

cat > scripts/setup-permissions.py << 'SCRIPT'
import discord, os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, '.')
from src.discord.intents import get_intents

async def setup():
    token = os.environ.get("DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN", "")
    client = discord.Client(intents=get_intents())
    
    @client.event
    async def on_ready():
        guild = client.guilds[0]
        bot_member = guild.me
        
        for channel in guild.text_channels:
            # Bot can read and write everywhere
            await channel.set_permissions(bot_member, 
                read_messages=True, send_messages=True, 
                embed_links=True, attach_files=True,
                read_message_history=True)
            print(f"Set permissions for #{channel.name}")
        
        await client.close()
    
    await client.start(token)

asyncio.run(setup())
